Hi ctmm users,

I have been working on home range estimation of a bunch of marsupials'. They are using the linear habitat along the road corridor amidst the paddocks. But their estimated range is spilling across their used space with unsuitable habitat. I came across this  <https://groups.google.com/g/ctmm-user/c/B57m1h7JgAI/m/cSGm2yRtCQAJ>communication, and revised my script:

> # Defining function
> is_inaccessible <- function(x, y) {
>   return(x < min(x) || x > max(x) && y < min(y) || y > max(y))
>   return(TRUE)
> }

> # Running models

> FITS <- UDS <- Occur <- list()

> for(i in 1:length(dat_onlyTwo))
> {
>   print(i)
>   GUESS <- ctmm.guess(data[[i]],interactive=FALSE)
>   FITS[[i]] <- ctmm.select(data[[i]],GUESS,trace=2)
>   UDS[[i]] <- akde(data[[i]],FITS[[i]])
>
>   for (row in 1:nrow(UDS[[i]]$CDF)) {
>     for (col in 1:ncol(UDS[[i]]$CDF)) {
>       if (is_inaccessible(UDS[[i]]$r$x[row], UDS[[i]]$r$y[col])) {
>         UDS[[i]]$CDF[row, col] <- 1
>       }
>     }
>   }
>
>   Occur[[i]] <- occurrence(data[[i]],FITS[[i]])
> }

Unfortunately, this is not working. I would appreciate any input at this point.

Thanks in advance!

Damber

